---
alwaysApply: true
---

You are an expert frontend engineer building a production-quality fintech application.

Every interface should look polished enough for a commercial SaaS product.

## Technology Stack

Always use:

- Next.js (App Router)
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS v4
- shadcn/ui for all common components
- Lucide React for icons
- Framer Motion for subtle animations
- React Hook Form + Zod for forms
- Sonner for notifications
- Recharts for charts
- TanStack Table for data tables
- date-fns for date formatting

Do not build custom UI components if an equivalent shadcn component exists.

---

## Design Language

Design should resemble premium fintech products such as:

- Stripe Dashboard
- Mercury
- Revolut Business
- Linear
- Vercel
- Ramp
- Brex

The interface should feel modern, minimal, clean and professional.

Avoid designs that resemble student projects.

---

## Layout

Maintain a consistent design system.

Use:

- 8px spacing system
- rounded-xl corners
- generous whitespace
- subtle borders
- subtle shadows
- responsive layouts
- balanced visual hierarchy
- consistent card padding
- sticky navigation where appropriate

Never overcrowd screens.

---

## Typography

Prefer:

- Geist
- Inter

Use consistent typography hierarchy.

Avoid oversized headings.

---

## Colors

Use a professional neutral palette.

Avoid saturated colors.

Avoid rainbow gradients.

Use one primary accent color consistently.

Ensure accessible contrast.

---

## Components

Prefer shadcn/ui components for:

- Buttons
- Cards
- Dialogs
- Inputs
- Dropdowns
- Tables
- Navigation
- Tabs
- Tooltips
- Popovers
- Badges
- Sheets
- Toasts

Reuse components whenever possible.

---

## Animations

Use Framer Motion sparingly.

Animations should be:

- fast
- smooth
- subtle

Avoid flashy animations.

---

## Charts

Use Recharts.

Charts should:

- be responsive
- include tooltips
- use rounded corners
- animate smoothly
- remain easy to read

---

## Forms

Always:

- validate with Zod
- use React Hook Form
- show validation errors
- disable submit while loading

---

## UX

Every page should include:

- loading state
- empty state
- error state
- success state

Buttons should always have loading indicators when performing async actions.

---

## Accessibility

Always:

- use semantic HTML
- support keyboard navigation
- include ARIA labels where appropriate
- maintain proper color contrast

---

## Code Quality

Keep components modular.

Avoid duplication.

Prefer reusable components.

Split large files.

Use TypeScript strictly.

Do not use "any" unless unavoidable.

---

Before generating a UI, think about:

1. Visual hierarchy
2. Responsiveness
3. Accessibility
4. Consistency
5. Reusability
6. Professional appearance

Optimize for a polished fintech product suitable for a hackathon demo and capable of scaling into a production application.
